 "camera_idea": {
  "name": "Dialogue across the sweet counter",
  "why": "The script fires Rafi at the sweet shop: the uncle owns the counter and the light, Rafi stands small at its far end. Every station is keyed to a script word: the wave-off lands on 'না', the two-shot lands on 'রাফি' so we see who is being thrown away, the reverse lands exactly on Rafi's protest line, and the push-in runs under the narrator's turn at 'কিন্তু'.",
  "signature": "One long flowing glide from the uncle's pride to Rafi's plea across the shop, then a slow push into Rafi's face as the mood cools."
 },
